hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1509","On the authority of Abu Ammar al-Hasan ibn Harith, on the authority of al-Fadl ibn Musa, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid ibn Jaafar, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Ataa, a mawla Abu Ahmad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent a group of people, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called them. He said hello and said: “What do you have of the Qur’an?” So he studied with them, until he passed by a man among them who was one of the youngest among them in age. He said: “What is the matter with you, so-and-so?” He said: I have such-and-such, and Surat Al-Baqarah. He said: “Do you have Surat Al-Baqarah?” He said: Yes. He said: “Go, for you are their prince,” and a man who was one of the most noble of them said: And such-and-such, O Messenger of God, has not prevented me from learning. The Qur’an except for fear that I would not recite it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Learn the Qur’an, then read it, and lie down; for the likeness of the Qur’an For whoever learns it, reads it, and performs it, it is like a sack stuffed with musk, the smell of which spreads everywhere. And whoever learns it, and sleeps inside it, it is like a \"A pod that I lean on.\""
